error[NK2209]: `slow` can pause, but this runs on several cores at once.
   --> tests/par_iter_pausing_fold_step_names_map_then_fold.nika:14:59
    |
 14 |     let sum = xs.par_iter().fold(fn() { 0 }, fn(acc, x) { acc + slow(x) }, fn(a, b) { a + b })
    |                                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: Only the lambda of a `par_iter()` chain's `map`, `filter` or `for_each` may pause, and runs one task per element; this one runs on every core at once, and a core that waits holds up its share of the work, so it must never pause (ADR-async-5 D29).
    = help: Call `slow` in a `map` before this step, whose lambda may pause: `xs.par_iter().map(…).fold(…)`. Or call it before the walk and pass the values in.
1 call that can pause where nothing may
